{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1192602-the-other-from-chronicler-s-guide","id":1192602,"title":"The Other - from Chronicler's Guide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-07T07:22:28-08:00","id":1192602,"title":"The Other - from Chronicler's Guide","content":"So in the Chronicler's Guide on pg. 59 they detail an alternative to the Beast - the Other.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo I have three players - two vampires and a mortal - my idea was to incorporate this into the game. My idea was to have one vampire with the standard Beast, the other vampire with the Other, and then have the mortal have a ghost of his dead friend inhabiting him. <br /> <br /> \u200bCan anyone give me any advice on how to run this? <br /> <br /> \u200bSo I should detail out two NPC's (dead girl and the Other - Beast isn't talking) along with their dialogue? The book suggests no more dialogue than once or twice per scene.<br /> <br /> Anything mechanical I should be aware of?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T07:57:17-08:00","id":1192609,"title":"","content":"Do what ever works best for your game! I think you should outline there basic personalty and general responsess but not in to much detail a plan never survives contact with your players! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T03:21:31-08:00","id":1193034,"title":"","content":"You might want to outline a few simple Aspirations, even for the Beast. Yes, it is more Savage, but you can still add some nuance there that makes it seem like another character too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T06:12:36-08:00","id":1193082,"title":"","content":"Is this first or second edition? 2e made the Beast a bit more rational than 1e. As said above do whatever works best for your chronicle but be mindful that those rules assumed 1e rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]